WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:07.050
I wonder what it will be?  
This week, it's this!

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:13.170
By releasing this card, that turn's 
battle damage becomes zero!

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.010
Zero, just like its name.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
I see.  This used to be 
Moment's research area.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.290
Who are they?

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.290
My turn!

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.470
You drew a monster card.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:01:01.050
At this moment, my Continuous Spell 
Destiny Activator's effect activates!

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:04.260
If you draw a card that's 
the same type as the card

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:08.260
that I sent to the graveyard, 
your life points are halved!

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:17.360
Yusei!

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:37.660
Looking over a vast distance

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:42.760
I realized my field of vision was narrow

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:47.670
Even if it's easier to throw myself away

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:52.440
I want to survive to the best of my abilities

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.800
No matter how bad today is

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.780
There's still the faintest light

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:08.190
All I have to do tomorrow

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:12.250
Is light it myself

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.260
I test myself so I won't stop or vanish

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:22.230
Even if I get countless scars

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:28.530
I ride wishing for the 
arrival of a true tomorrow

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.510
Today will never exist again

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:38.410
So I won't stop or vanish

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:08.050
Darkness in the Heart
The Final Remaining Hope

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:11.230
Looks like this is the end.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:16.860
This is bad!  Yusei only 
has 50 life points left!

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:22.050
I haven't run out of life points yet!

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:22.940
Yusei!

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:23.660
Hang in there!

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:24.510
Yusei!

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.720
I summon Zero Gardna in defense position!

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.960
Then I set one card and end my turn.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:35.430
So you still want to fight.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:38.900
You inherited your father's stubbornness.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:43.630
I can't believe that after 
17 years, the Signer

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:47.430
who has come to defeat me 
is Professor Fudo's son.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.740
I can feel the power of destiny.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:52.440
There's no destiny between us!

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.450
Stop acting tough.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.060
Your life points are like 
a candle in the wind.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:01.420
Your soul will soon vanish 
inside Moment's light.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.890
But before that, I'll tell 
you about your father.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:13.230
17 years ago, Professor Fudo was a quantum 
physics expert and discovered planetary particles.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.030
Planetary particles?

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:15.930
What's that?

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:23.940
Planetary particles act like planetary 
gears and tie other particles together.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.590
The professor named his 
son after this discovery.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:34.010
He wanted you to become the bond 
that ties strangers together.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:40.490
Planetary particles were new particles 
that were essential in creating Moment.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:43.740
The professor developed his theories and

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:47.040
started building Moment, a 
non-polluting energy engine.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.750
At that time, Rex and I were researchers.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:54.690
We were impressed with the professor's 
research and served as his assistants.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:59.940
Like a young boy, the professor spoke 
excitedly about his research's potential.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.000
He believed Moment would 
create a great future world.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:08.030
The research proceeded smoothly… 
until that incident.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.990
What's that sound?

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:19.010
The energy gauge is showing unusual numbers.

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.970
But there's nothing wrong with the equipment.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.120
We didn't know the cause.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:31.180
But we never thought that Moment 
would create unprecedented events.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:36.670
Every time we did a test, there 
was strange weather in the City.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:40.220
Professor, are you serious 
about stopping the tests?

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.680
We have no choice.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.790
Even though we don't know 
the cause, we know there's a

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.190
connection between Moment and the 
strange happenings in the City.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.790
But what about all our research?

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:50.490
I know.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:56.000
But if we can't guarantee their safety, 
we can't put the City people in danger.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.920
I researched data from around 
the world and found a place

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:05.220
where strange events occurred 
at the same time as the tests.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:15.040
It was the Nazca lands.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:23.030
I heard of a legend that the gods battle 
every 5000 years at the Nazca lands.

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:26.460
The Nazca Lines are evil 
gods that were sealed away.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:30.840
They battle against heaven's god 
dragon for control of the world.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.560
That's when I met a man.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.520
A man from Iliaster.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:44.250
Iliaster?

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:50.690
Professor Rutger, it's too bad that 
Moment research has been stopped.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.520
How did you know that?

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:58.220
I know that you want to 
continue the research.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.260
Am I wrong?

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:04.670
The research should be continued, even 
if that means removing Professor Fudo.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:06.880
No way!  What are you talking about?

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:12.040
There's potential beyond the Moment's 
light that you can't even imagine.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:15.180
Don't you want to see it?

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:22.680
Iliaster believes that you're the 
true genius who will rewrite history.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:28.030
Because you're the chosen one, Rutger Godwin.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.730
What do you mean?

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:32.330
The mark on your left arm.

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:39.070
I was born with this mark.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:42.370
That's right.  Destiny 
has already chosen you.

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:45.560
You can't escape your destiny.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.300
He has the mark of a Signer?

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.350
What does that mean?

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:56.350
Wait!

00:07:56.350 --> 00:08:01.640
The battle between the gods that 
occurs every 5000 years is real?

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:10.640
You'll have to see the will of 
Moment's light with your own eyes.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:26.570
The will of Moment's light…

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:58.620
I saw Moment's new potential!

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:06.730
Moment was chosen to resurrect 
the 5000 year-old gods.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.090
You're Godwin!

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:23.540
What are you doing here?

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:24.760
Crow.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:25.840
Answer me!

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:31.660
I came to say goodbye to my 
brother, my only blood relative.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:38.190
Since we were little, my brother was 
called a genius.  I'm proud about that.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:43.160
However, my brother carried the 
burden of unbelievable destiny.

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:47.390
No matter what you say, I'm 
stopping Moment's development!

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:51.170
Professor Fudo, you no 
longer have the authority.

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:55.480
You've just been expelled from MIDS.

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:56.670
What?

00:09:56.670 --> 00:10:00.680
How much money do you think we already 
paid for Moment's development?

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:03.070
We've already chosen your successor.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:06.850
Rutger?  What's the meaning of this?

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:13.690
Professor Fudo, since you don't have the 
courage to see the truth, I'm fulfilling your role.

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:17.390
I already made safety devices for Moment.

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:18.800
You can't operate it unless 
you break the seals-

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.200
When you say seals…

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:22.170
Do you mean these?

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:25.160
That's…

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:29.320
Don't let him escape!

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:40.520
Pull yourself together, Professor Fudo!

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:44.490
Rex, stop Moment.

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:48.460
Take these cards.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.850
Brother, where are you?

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.150
Brother!

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:22.100
What's wrong, brother?

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:26.760
Rex.

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:30.660
People known as Signers 
will eventually appear.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:34.940
No matter how many years it takes, 
gather them and defeat me!

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:36.770
What are you talking about, brother?

00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:38.610
Do as I say, Rex!

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:43.190
Two gods live inside my body.

00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:45.850
But I select the path of the evil god!

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:51.320
Take this and escape while 
I still have my sanity!

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:52.790
Brother!

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:54.400
Go!

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:15.980
I will be reborn as a Dark Signer!

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:59.070
That's when the gates to the 
underworld opened after 5000 years.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:06.260
Due to that accident, Jack, Yusei and my parents 
died, and City and Satellite were split into two.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:12.100
Even the legendary man was unable to stop 
the split between City and Satellite.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:16.060
You know the man who flew 
from Daedalus Bridge?

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:19.970
No, but I've never forgotten his dream.

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:23.150
Someday, I'll unite City 
and Satellite into one.

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:29.280
You have the same goal as Yusei.

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:31.860
Give Yusei a message for me.

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:36.710
If he defeats my brother, I'll be waiting.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:37.930
Wait!

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:40.130
What does that mean, Godwin?

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.350
That's why you're pretending to be god?

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:47.600
How many lives will you play 
with until you're satisfied?

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:54.310
Yusei, by the time I knew my destiny, 
the gods were already in my hands.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:57.610
I chose to have darkness in my heart.

00:13:57.610 --> 00:14:02.770
This world will soon be 
reborn!  That's my answer!

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.630
My turn!

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:08.820
Yusei, I have to keep moving ahead!

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.400
Go, Earthbound Immortal Uru!

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:13.350
Attack Yusei directly!

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:16.400
Zero Gardna's effect activates!

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:24.240
By releasing Zero Gardna, 
battle damage becomes zero!

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:27.160
You managed to stop my attack.

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:30.410
I set one card and end my turn.

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:33.490
If he gets directly attacked 
next time, he'll lose!

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:34.890
You have to trust Yusei!

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:36.320
My turn!

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:38.690
I set two cards.

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:41.640
What will he do next turn?

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:44.160
I end my turn.

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:47.430
Yusei, you're betting on that trap.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:50.140
Your only strategy is defense, Yusei?

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:51.870
My turn.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:56.440
With this, I'll kill your hope!

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.310
The spell card Earthbound Whirlwind!

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:05.090
When an Earthbound Immortal is on the field, all 
spell and trap cards on your field are destroyed.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:06.570
This is bad!

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:09.500
If his set cards are destroyed, 
Yusei will be wide open!

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.090
I was waiting for that!

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:13.490
I activate my trap Starlight Road!

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:16.420
Effects that destroy two 
or more cards are negated!

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:24.350
Then I'm allowed to Special 
Summon Stardust Dragon!

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:26.680
Appear, Stardust Dragon!

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:34.710
He did it!

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:38.150
He was able to block his opponent's 
attack and summon Stardust Dragon!

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:44.120
You've showed up, Stardust 
Dragon.  But it's too late.

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:45.530
I'm not done!

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:49.030
I activate the trap card Shooting Star!

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:53.340
When Stardust Dragon is on my 
field, I can destroy one card.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:57.300
I destroy your Field Spell Spider Web!

00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:00.550
That's not good enough, Yusei!  I 
activate the trap card Anti Emptiness!

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:03.240
By making one of my monsters' attack points

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:06.240
become zero, your spell or 
trap's activation is negated.

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:13.220
I end my turn.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:17.190
Earthbound Immortal's attack 
points return to 3000!

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:18.610
My turn!

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:21.670
I activate the spell card Battle Waltz!

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:27.270
I Special Summon one Waltz Token that copies a 
Synchro Monster on the field, except for its effect!

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:30.700
But Earthbound Immortal can't 
be the target of attack!

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:33.870
I'm aiming for you directly, Rutger!

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:36.140
Go, Waltz Token!

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:40.300
Did you forget that I have a Continuous Trap?

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:42.160
Roar of the Earthbound!

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:45.870
When a monster with fewer attack points 
than Earthbound Immortal attacks...

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:51.160
...that monster is destroyed, and you take 
damage equal to half that monster's attack points!

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.360
With this, I win!

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:55.730
I activate Stardust Dragon's effect!

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:57.460
Victim Sanctuary!

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:01.670
By releasing Stardust Dragon, the 
destruction effect is negated!

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:05.100
Go, Waltz Token!  Attack him directly!

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.570
Yusei will win!

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:10.230
Not yet!  I activate my 
trap Brilliant Shrine Art!

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:13.280
Earthbound Immortal intercepts your attack!

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:15.240
Uru has 3000 attack points!

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:17.970
It's over for you, Yusei.

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.990
But there's nothing to be ashamed about.

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:24.430
We have written an incredible 
page for the history books.

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:41.040
Too bad.  When Waltz Token is destroyed, 
both players take zero battle damage.

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:41.690
What?

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:43.810
Waltz Token's effect!

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:46.420
When your monster destroys 
this Token in battle,

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:49.420
its attack points decrease 
by the Token's attack points!

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:53.050
Rutger!

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:56.060
I don't care about your destiny!

00:17:56.060 --> 00:18:02.320
You forgot that the madness you call destiny 
destroyed the lives of many people!

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:06.300
The survivors had to face enormous struggles!

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:12.800
If my father didn't do research, the 
accident 17 years ago wouldn't have happened.

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:16.360
That accident took the lives 
of Jack and Crow's parents.

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:19.730
It messed up everyone's lives!

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:26.400
If it never happened, they would have 
caring parents and lived peaceful lives!

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:31.090
But they still regard me as their friend!

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:33.950
They smile at me without saying a word!

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:36.860
What am I supposed to do?

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:39.590
How am I supposed to atone for them?

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:41.630
Yusei…

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:43.390
Answer me!

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:45.000
Answer me, Rutger!

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.840
That's the darkness in your heart.

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:52.310
I'll give you an answer, Yusei!

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:57.750
Crow...

00:18:58.350 --> 00:19:02.750
Yusei, I didn't know you were 
burdened with those feelings.

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:04.610
I'm sorry.

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:09.090
I'm your friend.  I should've noticed.

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:10.290
Crow...

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:16.980
But Yusei, I never thought for a second 
that you or your father ruined my life!

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:20.270
So you don't need to feel responsible!

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:27.390
If I believed in destiny, it 
would only be about meeting you!

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:32.020
Only about meeting you and Jack, 
two irreplaceable friends!

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:35.090
Yusei, win for us!

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:36.870
Crow…

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:43.980
Rutger, your deranged light 
won't brighten my heart!

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:46.310
My irreplaceable friends will!

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:51.070
And in this duel, this is the 
final hope remaining on my field!

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:54.740
I flip over the trap card Stardust Flash!

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:58.360
On the turn Stardust Dragon was 
released due to its own effect,

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:01.320
I can Special Summon Stardust 
Dragon from my graveyard!

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:09.320
Stardust resurrected?

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:13.280
Go, Stardust Dragon!  Shooting Sonic!

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:32.800
Don't think that it's over.

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:36.730
The new mightiest god has already been freed.

00:20:36.730 --> 00:20:37.510
What?

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:42.050
If you haven't activated the safety 
devices in the four towers by sunset...

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:46.490
...the gates to the underworld opens, and 
the King of the Underworld resurrects!

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:48.220
King of the Underworld?

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:52.880
Yusei, I won't let you leave!

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:00.050
Yusei!

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:01.500
Yusei!

00:21:58.250 --> 00:22:02.720
We look up and vow towards the shining light

00:22:03.080 --> 00:22:07.790
We will build our own future

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:13.230
The far dawn shines blindingly

00:22:13.690 --> 00:22:18.400
Awaken in the wonderland

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:33.540
The overflowing wave of emotions approaches

00:22:33.970 --> 00:22:39.110
This world can't be solved using algorithms

00:22:39.180 --> 00:22:43.820
Even if it loses its light

00:22:44.290 --> 00:22:49.090
The hourglass behind the 
heart can't be turned

00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:53.560
Roll the dice and get 
out and follow the light

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:59.140
Fly towards tomorrow faster than a heartbeat

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:04.020
This journey has no end

00:23:04.240 --> 00:23:09.480
There's no meaning because there are no tears

00:23:09.910 --> 00:23:14.720
